CRITERION 2 — Behavior unchanged, byte for byte; the passphrase branch still
returns exactly "failed to decrypt SSH key: encrypted SSH keys require
passphrase decryption support (not yet implemented)". Asserted on the string.
MET.

Method: exported both trees (`git archive 7fe9b98^` -> <scratch>/pre,
`git archive 7fe9b98` -> <scratch>/post) and dropped the SAME in-package harness
(harness_p17_test.go) into internal/services/storage in each. The harness calls
the exported API (NewSSHProvider + Unlock) and logs the raw error text, so it
compares observable behavior, not code shape. Three cases:
  A. passphrase-protected key file, Unlock("somepassphrase")
  B. plain valid ed25519 key, Unlock("somepassphrase")  (the branch under change)
  C. plain valid ed25519 key, Unlock("")                (the untouched success path)

`go test ./internal/services/storage/ -run TestP17ErrStringHarness -v` on PRE:
  CASE_A_ERR>>>failed to decrypt SSH key: encrypted SSH keys require passphrase decryption support (not yet implemented)<<<
  CASE_A_NIL>>>false<<<
  CASE_A_UNWRAP>>>encrypted SSH keys require passphrase decryption support (not yet implemented)<<<
  CASE_B_ERR>>>failed to decrypt SSH key: encrypted SSH keys require passphrase decryption support (not yet implemented)<<<
  CASE_B_NIL>>>false<<<
  CASE_C_ERR>>><nil><<<
  CASE_C_NIL>>>true<<<
Same command on POST produced the identical six lines.

`diff <scratch>/pre.out <scratch>/post.out` reported one differing line and only
one:
  10c10
  < ok  budget2/internal/services/storage  0.008s
  ---
  > ok  budget2/internal/services/storage  0.004s
i.e. the go test wall-clock line. Every CASE_* line is byte-identical, including
the errors.Unwrap chain (CASE_A_UNWRAP), so `%w` wrapping is preserved and
errors.Is/As behavior is unchanged. The literal in the criterion matches the
produced string exactly.

Recorded as a note, not a failure: the new branch returns
`fmt.Errorf("failed to decrypt SSH key: %w", err)` unconditionally, so if
decryptSSHKey were ever implemented to succeed it would format a nil error as
`%!w(<nil>)` rather than continuing. That is latent, not current: the stub at
internal/services/storage/ssh_provider.go:102-107 has a single return statement,
`return nil, fmt.Errorf("encrypted SSH keys require passphrase decryption support (not yet implemented)")`,
and staticcheck itself confirms it "never returns a nil interface value". Today's
behavior is identical, which is what criterion 2 asks.

