CRITERION 4 — No other caller depended on the removed assignment. Established by
search.
MET.

The removed statement was `keyData, err = decryptSSHKey(keyData, []byte(p.passphrase))`
— an assignment to a function-local variable inside (*SSHProvider).loadIdentity.

  grep -rn "decryptSSHKey" --include="*.go" .
Excluding the two stale .claude/worktrees copies (not part of the build; they are
the tier-3 arm worktrees), the only hits in the tracked tree are:
  internal/services/storage/ssh_provider.go:81   (the single call site, in loadIdentity)
  internal/services/storage/ssh_provider.go:101-102 (the definition)
  internal/services/storage/ssh_provider_test.go:246 (TestDecryptSSHKey)
No other production caller exists.

  grep -n "keyData" internal/services/storage/ssh_provider.go
  69:  keyData, err := os.ReadFile(p.keyPath)
  81:  _, err := decryptSSHKey(keyData, []byte(p.passphrase))
  85:  identity, err := agessh.ParseIdentity(keyData)
  210: keyData, err := os.ReadFile(keyPath)   <- unrelated local in DetectSSHKeys
  215: keyStr := string(keyData)              <- same unrelated local
The only downstream consumer of loadIdentity's keyData is agessh.ParseIdentity at
line 85, which is reachable only when p.passphrase == "" because the passphrase
branch now returns unconditionally. Confirmed empirically by harness CASE_C
(passphrase == "" -> CASE_C_NIL true, identity parsed, no error) on both trees.

Callers of loadIdentity: `grep -rn "loadIdentity" --include="*.go" .` shows
ssh_provider.go:143 (Unlock) as the sole caller of the SSH one; the other hits are
the independent AgeProvider.loadIdentity and YubiKeyProvider.loadIdentity methods
and their tests, which do not touch this code.

